# Build context exclusions.
#
# The mcp-server image uses the repository root as its context so it can reach
# both rust/ and typescript/. Without this file that means shipping EVERYTHING to
# the daemon -- a local test build transferred 14 GB before it got to the first
# instruction, nearly all of it rust/target and node_modules. In CI that is a
# slow job at best and a failed one at worst.

# Build outputs — regenerated inside the image, never wanted from the host
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Caches
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.cargo/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Agent + editor scratch
**/.mimosa/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# VCS and CI metadata: the build does not read them, and .git alone is large
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Docs and analysis — none of it is needed to build a binary or an image
docs/
evidence/
testvectors/
**/*.md
!README.md

# Local state that must never end up in an image
.auditvenv/
**/.env
**/*.log
